"""
analysis.py -- solution-phase electron-transfer response calculation.

Reads data/ and writes required outputs under results/.

Scientific conventions (fixed by contract, plus documented choices):
  * Raw coordinate/Hessian rows are frame-specific (frame row order). Every
    scored 21-vector (7 sites x xyz) and retained basis is reported in
    ascending site_id order; the per-frame row->site map comes from
    data/frame_site_order.csv.
  * Directions ordered FORWARD = frame B viewed in frame A, BACKWARD = frame A
    viewed in frame B.
  * Signed displacement-like outputs use "aligned source - reference target"
    (forward: aligned B - A; backward: aligned A - B). Projected displacements
    and signed modal coordinates preserve that direction convention.
  * Cross-frame overlaps and transported profiles are MAGNITUDE-based with
    respect to eigenvector sign (sign-agnostic form uses |O| and |p|).
  * dominant_mode_forward/backward are zero-based retained-mode indices.

Documented column semantics of the underspecified arrays:
  * mode_projection.npy (2,15,3): [direction, retained mode of target frame, col]
      col0 = frequency nu (cm^-1) = sqrt(lambda_omega2)*freq_scale
      col1 = signed mass-weighted modal displacement p (source - target)
      col2 = reorganization contribution 0.5*omega^2*p^2 (eV); sum = lambda_nm
  * transported_mode_projection.npy (2,15,2): [direction, retained target mode, col]
      col0 = signed transport of source projection into target basis via
             frame-consistent overlap O (t_m = sum_j O[m,j] p_src_j)
      col1 = magnitude transport (|O| @ |p_src|), eigenvector-sign insensitive.

The figure overview.png is produced with matplotlib when available, otherwise
with the self-contained pure-Python PNG renderer embedded below.
"""
import json
import math
